{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>They shall divide it as an inheritance.</b> A verb that takes two objects, and so too ונחלתנו, according to the grammarians." "<b>Eleazar.</b> First, because by his word Joshua went out; he too is a son of Aaron. And he did not mention a prince for the sons of Reuben and Gad, for they had already taken their portion. And the commentators said that he began with Judah because the lot came out first. Only there is a great objection against them, even though the interpretation is correct, as will be seen according to our view."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:19.184604024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}